1
00:00:02,197 --> 00:00:04,234
Now we're almost done. There is one last

2
00:00:04,282 --> 00:00:06,143
convenience feature which I wanna show you.

3
00:00:06,849 --> 00:00:08,260
Once you write more complex Deno

4
00:00:08,276 --> 00:00:10,682
applications, you'll have a lot of imports

5
00:00:10,682 --> 00:00:12,431
from the standard library or from

6
00:00:12,607 --> 00:00:13,553
third-party libraries.

7
00:00:14,387 --> 00:00:16,970
Now you can always add your imports like

8
00:00:17,034 --> 00:00:19,328
this in every file, and that's perfectly

9
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:19,649
fine,

10
00:00:20,242 --> 00:00:23,290
but you also can create a so-called import

11
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:27,011
map so that you can use shorter URLs or

12
00:00:27,059 --> 00:00:29,946
identifiers your code files and you have the

13
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,978
full URLs in those import maps.

14
00:00:34,277 --> 00:00:36,009
For this, you should simply create a new

15
00:00:36,105 --> 00:00:41,254
file which you can name import_map.json. The

16
00:00:41,334 --> 00:00:44,125
name is up to you, but the extension should

17
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:46,515
be JSON because you have to write some JSON

18
00:00:46,627 --> 00:00:47,141
code in there.

19
00:00:48,151 --> 00:00:50,814
And in here you can have an imports key,

20
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,166
and that imports key allows you to map

21
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:56,925
certain identifiers of your choice which are

22
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:57,889
your key names here,

23
00:00:58,499 --> 00:01:00,120
to full URLs.

24
00:01:00,666 --> 00:01:04,456
For example, we could map HTTP slash to

25
00:01:05,788 --> 00:01:08,679
this full URL. So we can grab—

26
00:01:09,321 --> 00:01:11,505
excuse me, this URL. So we can grab this

27
00:01:11,569 --> 00:01:12,002
URL,

28
00:01:12,773 --> 00:01:13,544
cut it from here,

29
00:01:14,234 --> 00:01:16,129
and instead specify it here as a string

30
00:01:16,241 --> 00:01:18,329
value for the HTTP identifier,

31
00:01:19,051 --> 00:01:20,609
and also add the slash here.

32
00:01:22,983 --> 00:01:25,773
With this, we're mapping this URL to the

33
00:01:25,853 --> 00:01:26,446
http://

34
00:01:26,975 --> 00:01:27,568
identifier.

35
00:01:28,258 --> 00:01:30,181
And in our file, we can now use

36
00:01:30,582 --> 00:01:34,285
http://server.ts like this, which of course

37
00:01:34,285 --> 00:01:35,023
is way shorter.

38
00:01:35,808 --> 00:01:37,892
But at the moment, Deno wouldn't be able to

39
00:01:37,892 --> 00:01:40,409
make the connection between this code file

40
00:01:40,682 --> 00:01:41,932
and our import map here.

41
00:01:42,862 --> 00:01:45,106
Instead, to allow Deno to make this

42
00:01:45,106 --> 00:01:47,687
connection, we have to run our script with

43
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,446
deno run,

44
00:01:49,354 --> 00:01:51,103
allow net of course, and then

45
00:01:52,755 --> 00:01:54,002
import_map

46
00:01:54,618 --> 00:01:56,334
equals and then your map name,

47
00:01:56,884 --> 00:02:00,182
import_map.json. And at the moment you're

48
00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:02,688
only allowed to have one import map, but of

49
00:02:02,704 --> 00:02:05,517
course in there you can map as many packages

50
00:02:05,695 --> 00:02:08,443
as you want, as many modules as you want. So

51
00:02:08,443 --> 00:02:10,838
you're not limited to just one mapping here.

52
00:02:12,075 --> 00:02:14,373
So with that specified, we thereafter have

53
00:02:14,453 --> 00:02:14,678
our

54
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:16,836
filename. And if we now

55
00:02:17,462 --> 00:02:19,937
hit enter, we see that at the moment at

56
00:02:19,937 --> 00:02:22,620
least import map is an unstable feature.

57
00:02:23,391 --> 00:02:25,336
This means that it might change in the

58
00:02:25,336 --> 00:02:27,746
future. The way it works might change. For

59
00:02:27,746 --> 00:02:30,156
example, we might be able to have multiple

60
00:02:30,172 --> 00:02:31,297
import maps in the future.

61
00:02:31,988 --> 00:02:34,784
To unlock such unstable features, we have to

62
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,820
add one extra flag. As you also see here,

63
00:02:38,351 --> 00:02:40,681
we have to add the unstable flag.

64
00:02:41,483 --> 00:02:43,730
And with this, our file now executes

65
00:02:43,746 --> 00:02:46,041
successfully because of this map.

66
00:02:47,164 --> 00:02:48,673
Now what you'll also see though is

67
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:50,518
that at least currently

68
00:02:51,112 --> 00:02:54,306
my IDE isn't really able to pick up this

69
00:02:54,306 --> 00:02:56,665
map. It doesn't really understand this map,

70
00:02:57,211 --> 00:02:59,746
and therefore whilst the code runs fine,

71
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,068
my IDE support isn't on the level I'd like

72
00:03:03,068 --> 00:03:03,469
it to be.

73
00:03:04,031 --> 00:03:06,535
Therefore, for the moment, and because this

74
00:03:06,535 --> 00:03:09,404
is unstable, I will not use import maps

75
00:03:09,404 --> 00:03:11,327
throughout the course, but you absolutely

76
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,731
could if you want to. That's why I want to

77
00:03:13,731 --> 00:03:15,894
show you this feature because of course it

78
00:03:15,894 --> 00:03:18,490
is very handy. It allows you to manage all

79
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:22,000
your URLs in one place and then just use

80
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,836
these aliases to import from there, which

81
00:03:24,948 --> 00:03:27,592
leads to shorter code here. And if you ever

82
00:03:27,592 --> 00:03:29,675
wanna change the version, you just have to

83
00:03:29,675 --> 00:03:32,287
do it in one place instead of all code files

84
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,351
where you are using library module. So

85
00:03:35,528 --> 00:03:38,161
import maps can be useful, but because the

86
00:03:38,161 --> 00:03:40,730
developer experience at the moment, because

87
00:03:40,746 --> 00:03:43,363
of the IDE not understanding it, is not on

88
00:03:43,395 --> 00:03:45,723
the level I want it to be, I will not use

89
00:03:45,723 --> 00:03:46,012
them here.

90
00:03:46,831 --> 00:03:48,870
Before I revert this back though, let me

91
00:03:48,934 --> 00:03:50,893
also show you how to make it work with

92
00:03:51,086 --> 00:03:51,471
Denon.

93
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,120
There, of course, you now simply have to add

94
00:03:54,153 --> 00:03:55,293
this extra argument here

95
00:03:55,822 --> 00:03:56,497
where you have

96
00:03:57,027 --> 00:03:57,813
unstable

97
00:03:58,391 --> 00:04:01,954
and where you have import map endpoint at

98
00:04:02,483 --> 00:04:04,505
import_map.json.

99
00:04:05,147 --> 00:04:06,735
With that, you would be able to run this

